HTH.</span></span></span></span></div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Sun, May 6, 2018 at 6:40 AM Edina Shisue Miazaki &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mia...@unb.br</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif\">\r\n<p>Prof. Chalmers,</p>\r\n<p>In order to estimate 160 items parameters, I am using the function mirt.model as:</p>\r\n<p>mirt.model(&#39;F = 1 -160<br> PRIOR = (1 - 160, a1, lnorm, 0, 0.5),(1 - 160,g, norm, -1.386294, 0.5)&#39;)</p>\r\n<p>and it works fine.</p>\r\n<p>Since I have to run the program for different sets of items, with different number of items I tried:</p>\r\n<p>nItems=ncol(dataframe)</p>\r\n<p><span>mirt.model(&#39;F = 1 -nItems</span><br><span>PRIOR = (1 - nItems, a1, lnorm, 0, 0.5),(1 - nItems,g, norm, -1.386294, 0.5)&#39;)</span></p>\r\n<p>but it does not work. </p>\r\n<p><br></p>\r\n<p>Are there any ways I can fix this? I am working with only one factor and using all the items in the data frame.</p>\r\n<p><br></p>\r\n<p>Thank you.</p>\r\n<p><br></p>\r\n<p><br></p>\r\n<div>-- <br>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0;padding:0;font-family:monospace\">Edina Shisue Miazaki</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
